   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "hi all,\r<br>I am using the affy human promoter 1.0 array to analysis differential\r<br>methylation level between two group.\r<br>accoording to the vignettes: MAT - Tiling array analysis (Promoter 1.0R), I\r<br>get the MatSmoothing object:csMS. Although it could be loaded into IGB to\r<br>visualization by writeSgr(csMS). I still do not know the exact differential\r<br>region between two group where as the original MAT could generate. Anyone\r<br>could help me to figure this out? thanks\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>--\r<br>View this message in context: <a href=\"http://aroma-affymetrix.967894.n3.nabble.com/how-to-get-differential-region-after-MatSmoothing-tp4025138.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://aroma-affymetrix.967894.n3.nabble.com/how-to-get-differential-region-after-MatSmoothing-tp4025138.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793230467092000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2jy18jjnTDRK5qIPIvbn1-\">http://aroma-affymetrix.967894.n3.nabble.com/how-to-get-differential-region-after-MatSmoothing-tp4025138.html</a>\r<br>Sent from the aroma.affymetrix mailing list archive at Nabble.com.\r<br>"
