   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hello,<p>In the Bioconductor package Repitools, there is a function called regionStats. That will do what you need. You can find out more information at <a href=\"http://www.bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/Repitools.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/Repitools.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793230467094000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2SM3JAsMi3Kt_vX1ggJTOq\">http://www.bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/Repitools.html</a><br>________________________________________<br>From: <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">aroma-af...@googlegroups.com</a> [<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">aroma-af...@googlegroups.com</a>] on behalf of zhouzaiwei [<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">zhouz...@163.com</a>]<br>Sent: Wednesday, 14 August 2013 19:38<br>To: <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">aroma-af...@googlegroups.com</a><br>Subject: [aroma.affymetrix] how to get differential region after MatSmoothing?<p></p></p>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<p><p>hi all,<br>I am using the affy human promoter 1.0 array to analysis differential<br>methylation level between two group.<br>accoording to the vignettes: MAT - Tiling array analysis (Promoter 1.0R), I<br>get the MatSmoothing object:csMS. Although it could be loaded into IGB to<br>visualization by writeSgr(csMS). I still do not know the exact differential<br>region between two group where as the original MAT could generate. Anyone<br>could help me to figure this out? thanks</p></p>"
    ],
